 v.legend([['teal','true relation / predicate member'],['gold','selected step or edit cell'],['orange','false sentence']]);v.readout(()=>`${z.names[z.subject]} ${z.negative?'does not greet':'greets'} ${z.names[z.object]}: ${boolWord(z.truth)}. The object selects the relation column; the VP extension is {${z.extension.map(i=>z.names[i]).join(', ')}}. A curried verb combines with its object, then its subject; negation acts on the resulting proposition. Rows and columns are Ada, Bo, Cy. This finite lexicon has declared types and one relation; it does not parse arbitrary English.`);
